# REPRO: a governed seat that fits its BITS but not its DEMAND.
#
# The doomed-seat census measures a seat against `_seg_admission_need` — the
# group DEMAND in slots, which is what the DNUTS engine actually admits on.
# The HEALS that share the same arithmetic measured it in member BITS.  For
# an ungoverned bundle those are the same number, so the gap was invisible
# everywhere except on a governed bundle, where demand = bits + guards +
# shields.  A seat with room for the bits but not the shields therefore read
# as healthy, was never escalated, and stranded in full at DNUTS.
#
# ── The construction ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `shb` is `shield bus`: 4 bits flanked by 2 GND shields, so
#
#     bits   = 4        what the heals used to measure
#     demand = 6        what the engine admits on  (SBbBbBbBbS -> 6 slots)
#
# M9 carries a dense global pattern — which is what the PLANNER prices
# against — and a region override over the trunk that leaves ONE signal
# track per 40 units, so the seat's real pool is 5.  That is the #536
# supply-doomed shape: 5 >= 4 (the seat looks fine in bits) and 5 < 6 (it
# cannot host the run).  The override is the mechanism because a KEEPOUT
# would not do: the planner sees keepouts in its band capacity and simply
# routes elsewhere, so the doomed seat would never be chosen.
#
# M9 is the HIGHEST horizontal layer on purpose.  Equal-cost layers are
# enumerated highest-first, so the trunk lands on the starved one and M5 is
# left as the healthy re-seat target the heal needs.
#
# ── What must happen ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The TOP re-seat heal (`_final_reseat_heal`) sees a supply-doomed seat and
# moves the segment to M5, which can host all 6 slots.  Measured in bits it
# saw nothing to do and every bit stranded.
#
# The flow is deliberately HEALERLESS — no negotiate/ripup/refine — because
# the re-seat heal skips itself once any healer has run.  This vehicle is
# about that heal, so nothing else may pre-empt it.

add_block a 0   0 200  200
add_block b 900 0 1100 200

add_bus sh_[4] a.p b.q

def_layer 3 M3 V 20
def_layer 5 M5 H TOP 20
def_layer 6 M6 V TOP 20
def_layer 9 M9 H TOP 20

def_track_pattern 3 0 VDD 2 1 (_ 1 1)x12 GND 2 1
def_track_pattern 5 0 VDD 2 1 (_ 1 1)x12 GND 2 1
def_track_pattern 6 0 VDD 2 1 (_ 1 1)x12 GND 2 1
def_track_pattern 9 0 VDD 2 1 (_ 1 1)x12 GND 2 1

# The starved region: one signal track per 40 units over the trunk's span,
# invisible to the planner's global-pattern capacity model.
add_grid_override 9 200 0 900 200 0 CUSTOM 36 1 _ 1 1

def_ndr shb shield bus net GND
set_ndr sh_ shb

run_bundler STRICT
generate_topologies
set_track_pitch 3
run_planner 1

run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
dump_ndr
check_design
report_wirelength
